{
  "requirement": "For node reads, the SDK constructs a `Snapshot` from\nthe contents returned by `Domain::node_content` and their\n`NodeContents::fingerprint` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, without another read.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n\nimpl<T> Snapshot<T> {\n    pub fn new(content: T, fingerprint: Fingerprint) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<T: Clone> Clone for Snapshot<T>;\nimpl<T: Debug> Debug for Snapshot<T>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.snapshot`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. For node reads, the SDK builds a `Snapshot` from the contents returned by `Domain::node_content`.\n2. The snapshot's fingerprint is that content's `NodeContents::fingerprint`.\n3. No second read happens to build the snapshot.\n4. `Snapshot<T>` has public `content` and `fingerprint` fields, a `new` constructor, and `Clone` and `Debug` implementations.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- **Content and fingerprint pairing.**\n  - `tests/validation.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts that `read_snapshot(&1).fingerprint` equals `fp(\"before\")`.\n  - `tests/validation.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` asserts that `snapshot.content.format()` and `snapshot.fingerprint` match the original content. It covers an empty string and a large multi-byte Unicode string.\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` asserts that `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint`.\n- **No additional read.**\n  - The domain's mutable state is changed after the snapshot is taken. The tests then assert that the snapshot's content is still `before` and that its fingerprint is unchanged.\n  - The contracts test asserts that the read log is exactly `[1]`. The direct-read test asserts `[1, 1]`: one read for `read` and one for `read_snapshot`, so neither performs a second read.\n  - `tests/validation.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts the read log `[1, 1, 1, 2]`. That is one `node_content` call from the direct `graph()` use, one from `read`, one from `read_snapshot`, one from the second `read`, and one for the failing read of node 2. Each `ValidationContext` read performs exactly one `node_content` call.\n- **Agent read path.**\n  - `agent/tests.rs#fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` checks that the recorded `Dependency::Node` fingerprint carries the read content.\n  - `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` checks that `Dependency::Node` entries carry the matching fingerprints, in order and with repetition.\n- **Domain-level fingerprint.** `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` checks that a retained node content's fingerprint stays fixed after the underlying source changes. It also checks that the fingerprint of a fresh read differs.\n\n**Items without a dedicated test**\n- `Snapshot::new` is a pure pass-through of two fields.\n- `Clone` and `Debug` come from `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]`.\n- `#[non_exhaustive]` is an attribute.\n- None of these has a conditional or a transformation, so they fall under the untested pass-through exemption. `public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` also checks the exported surface.\n- The requirement does not say a value must stay unchanged, so the exemption's carve-out does not apply.\n\n**Assessment**\nThe fingerprint is computed from the retained content, not a re-read. Assertions on both the content and the fingerprint would fail if the snapshot used a different fingerprint or another read. I found no unacknowledged gap, and no acknowledgments were needed.",
